DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbssddiiffff utility compares _o_l_d_f_i_l_e to _n_e_w_f_i_l_e and writes to _p_a_t_c_h_f_i_l_e a
     binary patch suitable for use by bspatch(1).  When _o_l_d_f_i_l_e and _n_e_w_f_i_l_e
     are two versions of an executable program, the patches produced are on
     average a factor of five smaller than those produced by any other binary
     patch tool known to the author.

     The bbssddiiffff utility uses memory equal to 17 times the size of _o_l_d_f_i_l_e, and
     requires an absolute minimum working set size of 8 times the size of
     _o_l_d_f_i_l_e.

